# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=ADC
Version=aditf4_v3_0_G0_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
CommonClock|Common Clock|ADCgroup||||
FadcConstraint|Fadc Constraint|||1400000|48000000|
ClockPrescaler|Clock Prescaler|ADCgroup||||frequency of the clock to the ADC. The clock is common for all the ADCs.
EnableClockSemaphore|Clock Prescaler|ADCgroup||||
Resolution|Resolution|ADCgroup||||Resolution of the ADC conversion
DataAlign|Data Alignment|ADCgroup||||Select the alignment of the data stored after conversion.
ContinuousConvMode|Continuous Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Continuous Conversion Mode
DiscontinuousConvMode|Discontinuous Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Discontinuous Conversion Mode
DMAContinuousRequestsForConfigFile|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable DMA Continuous Requests
DMAContinuousRequests|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCgroup||||This parameter is used only when a DMA Request is configured. Else it is not relevant. When the DMA Request for this ADC instance this parameter specifies whether the DMA requests are performed in one shot mode (DMA transfer stops when number of conversions is reached) or are performed in continuous mode (DMA transfer unlimited, whatever number of conversions). Note: In continuous mode, DMA must be configured in circular mode. Otherwise an overrun will be triggered when DMA buffer maximum pointer is reached.
EOCSelection|End Of Conversion Selection|ADCgroup||||Regular channel end of conversion selection
Overrun|Overrun behaviour|ADCgroup||||Select the behaviour in case of overrun
LowPowerAutoWait|Low Power Auto Wait|||||Specifies the usage of dynamic low power Auto Delay: New conversion start only when the previous conversion (for regular channel) is completed.
NbrOfConversionFlag|Number Of Conversion Flag|ADCgroup||0|1|
NbrOfConversion|Number Of Conversion|ADCgroup||1|8|Number of regular channels to be converted
LowPowerAutoPowerOff|Auto Off|||||The ADC is always powered off when not converting and automatically wakes-up when a conversion is started
OversamplingMode|Oversampling Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable the over sampling mode
RightBitShift|Right Bit Shift|ADCgroup||||Configures the division coefficient for the Oversampler
Ratio|Ratio|ADCgroup||||Configure the Oversampling ratio
TriggeredMode|Triggered Mode|ADCgroup||||The regular triggered Oversampling mode
Sequencer|Sequencer|ADCgroup||||
SelectedChannel|ADC selected channels through mode list|ADCgroup||||
SamplingTime|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection
SAMPLINGTIME_COMMON1|Sampling Time common 1|ADCChannel||||
SAMPLINGTIME_COMMON2|Sampling Time common 2|ADCChannel||||
ExternalTrigConv|External Trigger Conversion Source|ADCgroup||||Select the external event used to trigger the start of conversion of a regular group
ExternalTrigConvEdge|External Trigger Conversion Edge|ADCgroup||||Select the external trigger polarity and enable the trigger of a regular group: When an external trigger is selected for ADC regular conversion, only the rising edge of the signal can start the conversion.
TriggerFrequencyMode|Trigger Frequency|ADCgroup||||ADC trigger frequency mode must be set to low frequency when a duration is exceeded before ADC conversion start trigger event (between ADC enable and ADC conversion start trigger event or between two ADC conversion start trigger event).
SamplingTimeCommon1|SamplingTime Common 1|ADCgroup||||Set sampling time common to a group of channels.
SamplingTimeCommon2|SamplingTime Common 2|ADCgroup||||Set sampling time common to a group of channels.
Channel|Channel|ADCChannel||||
Rank|Rank|ADCChannel||1|8|The rank in the regular group sequencer
ScanConvMode|Scan Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Scan Conversion Mode , To enable Scan conversion Mode : the number of Conversion should be > 1
ChannelVREF|ChannelVREF|||||
ChannelTS|ChannelTS|||||
ChannelVBAT|Channelvbat|||||
WatchdogMode2|Watchdog Mode|ADCgroup||||Configures the ADC analog watchdog mode.
WDG2MonitoredBy|Monitored by|Analog WatchDog 2||||For a dedicated channel, the generated analog watchdog configuration will correspond to the sum of all "Monitored" configurations for this channel when the number of ranks is greater than 1.
WDG3MonitoredBy|Monitored by|Analog WatchDog 3||||For a dedicated channel, the generated analog watchdog configuration will correspond to the sum of all "Monitored" configurations for this channel when the number of ranks is greater than 1.
WatchdogMode3|Watchdog Mode|ADCgroup||||Configures the ADC analog watchdog mode.
NbrOfChannel_WDG2CONV1|Number Of Channel can be monitored|Analog WatchDog 2||||Number of regular channels to be converted
